### SCENARIO: Duplicate request with same idempotency key
### Demonstrates that the system prevents double submissions
### Prerequisites: run 01-seed-balances.http first

### Step 1: Create a request
POST http://localhost:3000/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "emp-1",
  "locationId": "loc-nyc",
  "policyType": "VACATION",
  "startDate": "2026-11-01",
  "endDate": "2026-11-03",
  "days": 2,
  "idempotencyKey": "idempotent-001"
}

### Step 2: Send the exact same request again
# Expected: 201 but returns the SAME request (same id), no double balance hold
POST http://localhost:3000/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "emp-1",
  "locationId": "loc-nyc",
  "policyType": "VACATION",
  "startDate": "2026-11-01",
  "endDate": "2026-11-03",
  "days": 2,
  "idempotencyKey": "idempotent-001"
}

### Step 3: Verify balance — pending should be 2, not 4
GET http://localhost:3000/balances/emp-1/loc-nyc
